# AI & Inferencing Rules

## Model Configuration

- All model definitions live in `src/ai/models.ts` — NEVER hardcode model names or API URLs elsewhere
- Chat and summarization use `chatModel` / `summarizationModel` (OpenAI-compatible endpoint via `NAI_BASE_URL`)
- Embeddings use `embeddingModel` (Ollama `qwen3-embedding:8b`, 1536 dimensions)
- Environment variables: `NAI_BASE_URL`, `NAI_API_KEY` — never expose these in client code

## Agent Loop

The chat agent follows a structured loop in `src/ai/run-agent-loop.ts`:

```
User message → Select tools → Execute tools → Decide (continue or answer) → Generate answer
```

- `SystemContext` accumulates tool results across loop iterations — pass it through, don't recreate it
- Each tool execution streams status updates to the client via `OurMessageStreamWrite`
- The loop self-limits to prevent infinite cycles — respect the `maxIterations` parameter

## AI Tools

- Tool definitions live in `src/ai/tools.ts` using the Vercel AI SDK `tool()` helper
- Manual tool orchestration lives in `src/ai/actions.ts` (tool selection, decision-making, answer generation)
- ALWAYS validate tool inputs with Zod schemas — every tool must have an `inputSchema`
- Tool descriptions should be detailed and optimized for LLM understanding — guide the model on when and how to use each tool
- Search tools should instruct the LLM to rewrite queries for semantic matching, not use user queries verbatim

## Embeddings & Semantic Search

- Use `embedQuery()` from `src/ai/utils.ts` to convert text to embeddings — never call the embedding model directly
- Embedding vectors are 1536 dimensions — this must match the pgvector column definition
- Similarity searches use cosine distance (`1 - cosineDistance`) — higher scores mean more similar
- Always filter with a `minSimilarity` threshold to avoid returning irrelevant results
- The search flow is: text query → `embedQuery()` → `searchByEmbedding()` (in data-access)

## Summarization Pipeline

- Level 1: Summarize raw commits and issues per contributor per repo
- Level 2: Summarize a contributor's work within a repository (from Level 1 summaries)
- Level 3: Summarize a contributor's overall engineering profile (from Level 2 summaries)
- Scripts live in `src/scripts/summary/` — run with `pnpm summarize`
- Embeddings are generated separately with `pnpm embed`

## Avoid

- Don't call LLM APIs directly — use the exported models from `src/ai/models.ts`
- Don't create new tool definitions without adding them to the agent loop's tool mapping in `run-agent-loop.ts`
- Don't skip the use-case layer for search — embedding + DB query should be composed in `src/use-cases/`, not in tools directly
- Don't change embedding dimensions without updating both the model config and the database schema vector columns
